WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.822
The applied project combines several concepts.

00:00:02.822 --> 00:00:05.422
We sequence admissions for each patient.

00:00:05.422 --> 00:00:08.222
LAG retrieves the previous discharge.

00:00:08.222 --> 00:00:10.992
A second CTE calculates the gap.

00:00:10.992 --> 00:00:17.017
The final query joins patient names and classifies whether the new admission occurred within thirty days.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:20.472
This is a practical sequence-analysis pipeline.

00:00:20.472 --> 00:00:25.492
Connect this idea to a sales team calculating running revenue and top products by region.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:30.257
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:30.257 --> 00:00:36.797
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:36.797 --> 00:00:41.652
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:41.652 --> 00:00:46.780
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
